	<label  commandName="SimThermalLoadTipsAndTricksDesc" devLabel="To select all faces on a body, select a body or click &lt;b&gt;Select All Faces&lt;/b&gt; and pick any face.&lt;br&gt;For Surface/Internal Heat uncheck &lt;b&gt;Unit Area&lt;/b&gt; to specify the 'total' heat.&lt;br&gt;For Surface/Internal Heat check &lt;b&gt;Unit Area&lt;/b&gt; to specify a 'specific' heat per a unit volume, area or length.&lt;br&gt;For natural Convection (a buoyancy-driven flow with still air), use &lt;b&gt;Coefficient Value&lt;/b&gt; about 5 W/(m^2 C). Use a higher value to simulate faster flow.&lt;br&gt;For Radiation specify a value of &lt;b&gt;Emissivity/Absorptivity&lt;/b&gt; between 0 and 1. Use a lower value for reflective surfaces and a higher value for darker, emittive surfaces." translation="To select all faces on a body, select a body or click &lt;b&gt;Select All Faces&lt;/b&gt; and pick any face.&lt;br&gt;For Surface/Internal Heat uncheck &lt;b&gt;Unit Area&lt;/b&gt; to specify the 'total' heat.&lt;br&gt;For Surface/Internal Heat check &lt;b&gt;Unit Area&lt;/b&gt; to specify a 'specific' heat per a unit volume, area or length.&lt;br&gt;For natural Convection (a buoyancy-driven flow with still air), use &lt;b&gt;Coefficient Value&lt;/b&gt; about 5 W/(m^2 C). Use a higher value to simulate faster flow.&lt;br&gt;For Radiation specify a value of &lt;b&gt;Emissivity/Absorptivity&lt;/b&gt; between 0 and 1. Use a lower value for reflective surfaces and a higher value for darker, emittive surfaces." />
